A frontmatter key literally spelled `sp:gt` is not reachable by an `sp:gt=` clause — the suffix
is always dispatched as the ordering operator — so only the row carrying a plain `sp` matches,
even though both rows are discovered.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/plain/index.md --
---
title: Plain
sp: 5
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/shadow/index.md --
---
title: Shadow
"sp:gt": 5
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --output paths
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where sp:gt=1 --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/plain/index.md
plans/shadow/index.md
plans/plain/index.md
-- stderr --
